Subject: [PATCH 03336/11362] [outer-loop] arc: goal-bias v2
 (direction-agnostic, confirming) -- real cd82 unlock but the LEVER is REFUTED

ConfirmingGoalBiasValueHead: direction-agnostic extremality-on-any-axis pre-win + reads
frame.levels_completed to confirm the rewarded axis post-win (fixes v1's fixed-direction misroute).
Measured both modes + weight sweep:
- best_first: unlocks cd82 (1/11->2/11, a game undirected AND v1 both miss -- direction-agnostic
  signal is REAL) BUT best_first priority is pure-value (no depth term -> value_weight inert) and
  pays a ruinous replay-from-reset tax -> cd82 costs 1144 actions (~0 score); net SCORE worse.
- depth_first_ride (the efficient mode): value head INERT, identical to baseline at weights 1/5/20.
No regime improves the score: where the head has effect it tanks efficiency; where it preserves
efficiency it has no effect. The explorer-frontier-reordering lever is refuted for moving 0.08 --
the real first-win bottleneck is action-generation / mechanic-induction (the e3 LLM cascade, the
actual 0.08 mechanism), not the tier-1 explorer floor. Heads/policies preserved as refuted scaffolding.
Offline-first discipline worked: ~0 quota, exhaustive test, lever refuted, scarce shots SAVED.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
